# Stage 6 right clamp (D-075 visibility rule; game-design.md Stage 6
# "Difficulty and reach rules"): the solver route with RIGHT added from
# frame 560 on to every frame that doesn't hold LEFT (on the steamer the
# solver already drifts to the clamp; RIGHT there would walk her off its
# bow), so through the whole scroll Resi's hitbox stays at the right clamp
# (its left edge 242 px right of the camera from ~600 until the scroll ends
# at ~4050). Measured on this replay (first frame any part of the enemy's
# hitbox is on screen -> first frame it reaches the clamp line, where she
# can be touched): swans #1-#3 63 frames (they trigger as soon as they are
# fully on screen, 20 frames in, hiss 32, then charge; the sprite shows
# ~5 frames before the hitbox), Gelsen #1-#3 81-82 frames (60 frames
# hovering fully on screen, then the hunt), regatta boats #1-#3 85 frames
# (fully on screen ~30 frames in, then the 60-frame start). Swans and
# Gelsen never touch her here (she dives under the swans and outswims the
# Gelsen as the solver does); regatta #1 (3700) and #3 (3961) bounce her
# off their mastheads, 91 and 96 frames after they showed. No hurt, no
# death.
